# Profile overlay applied ON TOP of the pinned Firecracker v1.10.1 CI config.
# Every line here is a deliberate, measured deviation — keep it minimal.
#
# VIRTIO_MMIO_CMDLINE_DEVICES: Firecracker v1.10.1 describes the virtio-mmio
# devices BOTH in ACPI (DSDT) and on the kernel command line
# (`virtio_mmio.device=4K@0xd0000000:5`). Measured on this host, a kernel built
# from the unmodified pinned config fails ACPI table load
#   "ACPI Error: AE_BAD_PARAMETER, During Region initialization"
# and then finds no block device: "VFS: Cannot open root device vda ... -6".
# Reproduced identically with gcc 15.2 (host), gcc 12.5 (host) and gcc 12.2
# (debian:bookworm container), and for 6.1.102 built locally. Firecracker's
# OWN prebuilt vmlinux-6.1.102 (s3 spec.ccfc.min/firecracker-ci/v1.10) booted
# on the same host — so the difference is in their build, not the config text.
# Root cause NOT established.
#
# Mitigation (both needed, both measured):
#   1. this symbol, so the command-line device list is honoured, and
#   2. `acpi=off` on the guest command line (scripts/fc_linux_profile.sh),
#      without which virtio_blk probe fails with -EINVAL (-22) even with (1).
# Consequence: the guest runs WITHOUT ACPI (no ACPI power-off; shutdown is via
# `reboot=k` + i8042 reset, which Firecracker handles as VM exit).
CONFIG_VIRTIO_MMIO_CMDLINE_DEVICES=y
